  "description": "Interactive view of the infrastructure estate (datacenters, zones, subnets, firewalls, racks, ESXi, bare metal, VMs, OpenShift clusters, nodes, namespaces, pods) read from the relationship API. Pick a root object, a depth and a direction; one traversal call feeds every panel.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**Root** is where the walk starts, **Depth** how many relationship hops to follow, **Direction** which way: *down* = what the root contains or provides, *up* = what the root depends on, *both* = everything near it. Every panel below is a different view of the **same single API call** (`/traverse`). Double-click a node in the topology, or use *make root* in its details, to re-centre the whole dashboard on it."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Objects in view, by type",
